>>    - is there a workaround? (SO_REUSEADDR does not help, SO_KEEPALIVE
>>      checks only every 2..3 hours which is not fast enough)
> 
> We are having the same problem running perl 5.001 under Digital
> Unix 3.2D-1.  It usually takes 40 minutes for the connection
> to time out.  Nasty when inetd or some daemon is trying to
> re-use the port.  Any tips or patch numbers would be great.
> 

with some help from Christoph Robitschko <chmr@freebee.tu-graz.ac.at> we 
realized that the problem was caused by the fact that child processes
of the server were still alive. to get rid of this problem you should
either close the sockets you don't need (e.g. the listener) by hand after forking 
or - if you make an exec after the fork (like we did) simple 
	fcntl(socket,F_SETFD,FD_CLOEXEC)
this will ensure that the new process will close this socket while doing "exec".
works great for us.



