Hello,
I'm very disappointed about DEC Unix 4.0 and it's upgrade procedure. The
large amount of disk space in / was mentioned before. Old customization
were lost, e.g keyboard type or language settings. dxadvfs crashes with
segmentation fault. FrameMaker could't be exported to a X11R4-Server
anymore. (Xlib error of XPutImage). This was quite important for us, so I
did the following:
ar x libX11.a XPutImage.o       with dUnix 3.2's libX11.a
the same with 4.0's libX11.a in another directory
overwrite new PutImage.o with old XPutImage.o
ld -shared -expect_unresolved "*" -rpath /usr/shlib *.o -o libX11.so
cp /usr/shlib/libX11.so /usr/shlib/libX11.so.buggy
mv libX11.so /usr/shlib
shutdown -r now    (or restarting X11)

Quite simple isn't it ? The old host utility I compiled a while ago
makes core dumps now. Also the install scripts couldn't find our
Netscape 3.0beta in /usr/local/bin (what an unusual place !) and installed
Netscape 1.12 without asking. The same for Tk/Tcl.

Why do I have to edit config files just to make the german keybord layout
work correctly or to increase the number of saved lines in a DtTerm ? 
This were only a few mouse clicks on the preveous version. A telnet session
started in a DtTerm is a pain, even dUnix3.2 says "type dtterm unknown"

I looked twice on the box and the CD's but they don't call it "beta" or
"field test version" which it seems to be. 
All the above was found in just 48 hours, so I'm afraid that won't be all.
Why isn't there a /sbin/installdowngrade ??

Tschuess
Olaf

