That is great news.

Did DEC fix the bug in mcd? This was pointed out to me by one of my users: 
if you use
  mmd subdir
  mcd subdir
  mcd ..
then your ~/.mcwd file ends up containing 'a:/subdir/..' instead of plain 
'a:'. Thus you can confuse it badly if you also do
  mren subdir other
(which may in fact be a bug, since MS-DOS does not allow renaming of 
directories). Or you can blow MS-DOS's over-generous 128 character max 
pathname length if you often descend into directories and leave them with
'mcd ..'. And I am sure you can also confuse it simply by swapping floppies.
  
