------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Interactive Graph Visualization System daVinci V2.0 announced:
------------------------------------------------------------------------

June 24, 1996 (Bremen, Germany)  ---  The University of Bremen announces
daVinci V2.0,  the revised edition of the noted visualization system for 
generating high-quality drawings of  directed graphs with more than 1200 
installations worldwide.  Users in the commercial and educational domain 
have already  integrated daVinci as user interface  of their application 
programs for  visualizing hierarchies,  dependency structures, networks,  
configuration diagrams,  dataflows, and so on.  daVinci combines hierar-
chical  graph layout with powerful  interactive capabilities  and an API 
for remote access from a connected application.

Features at a glance:

  * Automatic graph layout with edge crossing- and bend minimization.
  * Interactive fine tuning for a given layout.
  * Many attributes for nodes and edges (color, font, shapes, ...).
  * Interactive abstractions (collapsing subgraphs, hiding edges).
  * Scaling operations for getting an overview.
  * Encapsulated PostScript output.
  * API for communication with an underlying application program.
  * Interactive graph editor as demo application.
  
What's new in daVinci V2.0:

  * Motif user interface: file browser, icon bar, keyboard support, etc.
  * Multi-graph and multi-view: many graphs in different windows.
  * Survey view to see a graph both in detail and overview.
  * Layout orientations: top-down, bottom-up, left-to-right, etc.
  * Vertical fine tuning: moving a node to another level.
  * Navigation features: browsing a graph in four directions.
  * Find operation to search for particular nodes.
  * 2D-scrolling: moving the focus simultaneously in both directions.
  * New attributes: nodes with double border, double and thick edges.
  * True color (24bit) for nodes and edges.
  * API-support for graph updates and attribute modifications.
  * Integrated help system and online documentation using Netscape.
  * New graph editor application to support new features.
  * 25% more performance, compared to daVinci V1.4.2.
  * Full compatibility with previous V1.x releases.
  
More information about daVinci is available in WWW:
  
  http://www.informatik.uni-bremen.de/~davinci
  
daVinci V2.0 is licensed free of charge  for non-profit use and is imme-
diately available for the following UNIX operating systems:  Sun Solaris 
2.x, SunOS 4.x, SGI Irix, DEC UNIX (aka OSF/1).  Distributions for Linux 
(ELF and a.out),  HP-UX, IBM AIX (3.x and 4.x) and  DEC Ultrix will come 
in July '96. The daVinci system can be downloaded from:

  http://www.informatik.uni-bremen.de/~davinci/daVinci_get_daVinci.html

There you can find  ftp-links to tar-archives (compressed with gzip) for 
all supported  OS platforms.  The content is the same  for all distribu-
tions, except of the binaries.  The sources are not available. Each dis-
tribution  covers daVinci,  the HTML online documentation,  examples and 
tools. To contact the daVinci project, to send bugs, to suggest new fea-
tures or to subscribe to the mailing list, please write by e-mail to: 

  daVinci@Informatik.Uni-Bremen.DE

