> I wish to find out if the Alpha is receiving data on its serial port.

I've setup an tcp/ip communication to the Ineternet via a serial port on
a OSF1 machine with no problems.

Generally, to see if anything is coming on the serial port, look at the
lamps on the modem: especially on the "receive data" (RD) and "transmit
data" (TD) lamps.

If this works you need some sort of program to receive the data. If it's
only ordinary text data, I guess you could use a terminal emulator, like
Kermit.

Otherwise, if you'd like to set up tcp/ip, use PPP or SLIP.

