Bill Hibbard wrote:
> So here is my question: do you know of anything I can do to
> control stack size for running Vis5D?  I need a larger stack.

You can control the size of the stack with the following tuneables in
/etc/sysconfigtab:

proc:
per-proc-stack-size
max-per-proc-stack-size

See the man page (section 4) on the sysconfigtab file.  To see what the
current values are, run the command: sysconfig -q proc.

This will increase the stacks on all processes, so it may have some side
effects (e.g. require more swap space if the system is in eager swap mode).

Pat

