>>>>> "Steve" == Steve Russell <stephen_russell@spectratek.co.uk> writes:

Steve>  I have an HP laserJet 5M ethernet printer (with Jetdirect
Steve>  card). It is set up to print postscript files. When a postscript
Steve>  file is sent to it there is no problem. However when I send an
Steve>  ascii file I get a postscript error on the printer. 
             
	[Printcap file snipped]

Steve>  As I understand the "if:" line should wrap any ascii files in
Steve>  postscript format before sending them off to the printer. I can
Steve>  only assume that this is not happening.  Does anyone have any
Steve>  ideas please .

  The filters are ignored if you print to a queue on a remote printer.
  It assumes that the remote printer will take care of any filtering you
  need.  

  Your options are to set up a second queue for text, using the line 
              
      :rp=text:

  in your printcap, or filtering the text file by hand before firing it
  at the printer:

     /usr/lbin/ln03rof < testfile | lpr -Plaser

  Neither solution is optimal. I would really like the printer to be
  able to switch by itself so that only one queue was necessary.

  Some people have suggested putting a wrapper around the lpr command to
  call ln03rof if the file is a regular text file.  This should work
  too. 

  Good luck,
		Phil


