Wuxu Peng <peng@infinite.cs.swt.edu> wrote:
}We are buying extra hard disks for our server 2100 5/250.
}Two choices: RZ29B-VW, which is faster and operates at
}7,200rpm, and RZ29B-VA, operating at 3,600rpm.
}However, it seems that in order for RZ29B-VW to be usable
}on 2100 5/250, additional converters/cases/cables are needed.

}Can someone tell me what are needed?  The Digital resellers
}gave me conflicting information.  Thanks a lot.

    The difference is the -VW variant is WIDE scsi,
    so you need a wide enclosure (e.g., BA356 vs BA350),
    wide cables (68 pins vs 50 pin), and a wide controller
    (e.g., KZPSA).  If you choose a differential (as opposed
    to single-ended) controller like the KZPSA you'll
    also need a differential-to-single-ended converter
    (e.g., DWZBB-VW).  Another controller option is the
    KZPSC-?? RAID controller (fast, wide, single-ended).

John
