Thanks for all who replied. The solution in this case came from
Curt Smith <curts@compgen.com> and was that I had to put the following 
into /etc/sysconfigtab:

   | vm:
   |     # Allows task image to grow larger than physical RAM, as long
   |     # as you have enough swap/virtual memory.
   |     vm-nowait-memalloc=1

this allows the process image to grow larger than the physical RAM.
what I still don't understand is why the default is vm-nowait-memalloc=0.



