The problem here is with the amount of memory you have in your video
board.  On my Digital Alpha, with 2 MB memory in video, the same problem
(and colors you describe) occurs when "too many" color intensive
processes are open.  For example, Netscape and a GIS (heavy duty
graphics) program cannot run simultaneously without color interference.
Your system will remap colors as best as it can.  There are two
solutions: 1. Get a video board with more memory (8 MB will do it) --
but this is expensive (I didn't do it).  - or - 2. Close color-intensive
applications when using another color-intensive application.  You could
decrease the screen resolution, but I consider that anti-productive in a
multi-tasking environment.  

Good luck!! - Andy Lazarewicz



