>trys to mount to the Novell volume (/sys3/nfs1) we get thid error:

>Cannot mnt PRC: RPC: port mapper failure_RPC:Timeout

This means that the NFS client can't contact the portmap service on the
server to request the port for the mount protocol.

In Unix parlance, you aren't running portmap on the server.  I have no
idea what the Novell equivalent is.

If you have packet filter configured, watching the network traffic with
tcpdump can be a big time saver. See the Digital UNIX FAQ for instructions.
