Sorry for the delay in responding.  It took me a while to find
out the status of these patch kits (since I'm 3000 miles from
the people who deal with them).

The official story is that:
	V3.2C systems should be patched with Patch ID OSF350-195.
	This is an updated version of the patch ID I mentioned
	earlier (OSF350-146).

	V3.2D systems should use Patch ID OSF360-350195.

	In "a week or so" there should be Patch IDs suitable
	for use with V3.2E and V3.2F.

The unofficial story is that all of these patch kits have exactly
the same contents, as far as I can tell, and there is no known
reason why you can't use the OSF360-350195 patch on a V3.2F system.
On the other hand, "Digital does not recommend the use of patches
meant for one release on a system running a different release."
In other words, we haven't tested the OSF360-350195 patch on a V3.2F
system and if it doesn't work, I didn't tell you to use it :-).

Finally, this whole saga ends at V3.2F.  V3.2G, when it ships,
will have essentially the same Web-server-related fixes as in
V4.0, and should not require any of these patches.

-Jeff



