Bobbi Fortune wrote:
> 
> Can anyone point me in the right direction or tell me how to get the
> arrow keys to recall previous commands in Digital Unix?
> 


In 'ksh':
 
sither 'set -o emacs' or 'export EDITOR=emacs' . "vi" can be substituted for
"vi" in both cases , but then the arrow keys do not work and you must use
the 'vi' hjkl direction keys.

In 'csh' "set editmode=emacs". Again, "vi" can be substituted if you do not
mind using hjkl keys.

Charlie

PS I *really* recommend using 'ksh' since it is the Posix shell. Csh is not
as rigorous in its behavior consistancy , especially between platforms and
tcsh is unsupported, leading to potential security problems as well as the
associated higher level of bugs. My comments are based on actual time spent
debugging both 'csh' and 'ksh' for Digital Unix. (I am told that the glob.c
nightmare has been rewritten for DU4.0 csh and that should help)

