Is anyone out there running NIS, AFS (the Andrew File System) and CDE 
(Common Desktop Environment) on Digital UNIX?  We're just in the process 
of installing a group of Digital servers and have found that much to our 
dismay, the CDE login program dtlogin will not authenticate a user with 
AFS; you just get told your password is wrong, and you get bounced back 
to the prompt.  We have been able to login via an xterm windows and then 
start CDE from the command line provided we are not already running a 
window manager, but this is a rather ugly kludge that our users won't 
tolerate.  Among other things, you can't log out if you start it 
that way, you have to kill it manually.  We've checked with both 
Transarc (the AFS people) and Digital, but no one seems to have been 
able to do it yet.  As CDE will be the default desktop in version 4.0 of 
the OS, I've got to believe that this is of interest at other AFS sites 
running Digital UNIX.  Any ideas?

