pej@chrh.org (Paul E. Jones) writes:

>Since installing our DEC Alpha 2000 into a network with two IBM RS/6000s, we've 
>been experiencing problems with NFS.

>On the DEC Alpha, we get the following errors occasionally:

>vmunix: NFS write error 70 on host thehill fh 9000a00 3000000 1000a00 6a2e141a 
>a499 a00 200 100

The error is pretty much what it implies.  The Alpha box sent a NFS write
request to server and got errno==70 back.

70 is ESTALE, which means that a file on the RS/6000, which had been opened
by the Alpha, is no longer there and has probably been deleted by the server
or some other client.  The error is passed back to the application,
so you can chase it down that way if you are still interested.

>Is anyone aware of a known problem or have suggestions about how to fix it?

More along the line of "known confusion".  More people have been confused
by the error than helped so its days may be numbered.

