crashing on boot is:

The kernel tunable: rt_preempt-opt=1

[snippette from my /etc/sysconfigtab]
# setting rt-preempt-opt=1 causes kernel to panic on boot w/ ASE installed
#
#generic:
#       rt-preempt-opt=1


I would suggest that the kernel/ASE kernel modules should be 
tolerant/knowledgable and ignore things that could cause even minor problems,
which includes anything that would cause a panic.  8-<

It took re-installing Unix on both boxes and lots of fooling around to
find this simple problem.

I'm viewing the slippage of DUX v4.0 as a good sign that problems like 
this will be caught by DEC and not me.


