Hi there,

We are doing exactly the same - porting from Solaris to Digital-UNIX
using the Sun and the Dec C++ compilers. I have done porting of more 
than 200000 lines of C++ code and have noticed the following:

The Dec compiler does a much stronger syntax check. We had actually more
problems on the Sun using templates. Another annoing thing of the
Sun complier is the prefix and the postfix operator ( i++ oder ++i for 
example ). The Sun complier does not seem to make any difference. 

Furthermore I'd go for the DEC C++ 5.3 which supports STL already.

The only drawback of the Dec compiler is that it seems to produce bigger
object files which result in a bigger imagesize.

Hope this helps

Juerg



