Kent Bloom (kent.bloom@mci.com) wrote:
: Hello,

: I am looking for a COBOL compiler which generates code optimized
: for the Alpha to run under OSF1.

: Does anyone have any suggestions, or experience with COBOL on DUNIX?

: We now have MicroFocus COBOL (which appears to have real performance
: problems, although it does create executables for a number of
: systems).

We have used both MicroFocus and DEC COBOL. One thing to look out for is 
the products that support COBOL, and which type of COBOL. Eg. we found that
Sybase only supports DEC COBOL, DCE works with either, Encina officially 
supports MicroFocus, etc. so building a system on one variant of COBOL may
not be as easy as you think. MicroFocus supports many C'ish things, like 
headers and function prototypes (which are nice but non-standard). It also has
an integrated development environment and debugger which is fairly standard
across platforms, whereas DEC's has the compiler, and the separate Ladebug 
debugger. There's seems to be more compiler switches on DEC COBOL to affect
alignment options for optimizing alpha code, versus portability from VAX COBOL.
and the -taso flago for porting 32bit programs to alpha.

Regards,

John De Angelis
Bankers Trust Australia





