In <4plend$7cf@aggedor.rmit.EDU.AU>,
  s9010721@minyos.its.rmit.EDU.AU (Aaron McDonough) writes:
>Hi,
>       Does anybody know how to restore files from magnetic tape to an
>NFS mounted disk and properly restore uid's and gid's correctly. Using tar
>(and gtar) the ownership is set back to nobody(the anonymous NFS user) 
>instead of the correct users. uid's and gid's are set correctly in the tar
>file and match those on the remote system, but the error still occurs.
>Does anybody know how to get around this problem?

That sounds like the filesystem is not exported with root access to the
client doing the restore - since presumably the restore is being done as
root, all the file accesses are performed as 'nobody' on the server, so
changing the owner may not be allowed.

>Any help will be *very much* appreciated.

Try one of:

  - export the filesystem with root access (there are of course security
    implications in doing this); see man exports or man exportfs for how
  - dd off the tape and pipe it into 'rsh serverhost tar xf -' or some
    approximate equivalent
  - execute on the server host 'rsh tapehost dd ....' piped into tar xf -
    (you get the idea)

There may be other variations on the above themes... :-)

HTH

