s9010721@minyos.its.rmit.EDU.AU (Aaron McDonough) writes:

>Hi,
>	Does anybody know how to restore files from magnetic tape to an
>NFS mounted disk and properly restore uid's and gid's correctly. Using tar
>(and gtar) the ownership is set back to nobody(the anonymous NFS user) 
>instead of the correct users. uid's and gid's are set correctly in the tar
>file and match those on the remote system, but the error still occurs.
>Does anybody know how to get around this problem?

>Any help will be *very much* appreciated.

>Cheers,
>	Aaron.

If you tar as root onto a NFS drive, which doesn't export with -root=0
you will be nobody to the NFS server. Solution: Either export the file
system with -root=0 (temporarily) or restore the files directly on the
NFS server machine. In both cases you need root privileges on the
server. 

Wolfram

