In article <SCOTT.96Jun17085539@death.dmi.stevens-tech.edu>,
Scott J. Kolodzieski <scott@death.dmi.stevens-tech.edu> wrote:
> Hello all,
  
> I just installed Digital Unix 3.2d and liscened everything, (we are at
> a univerity and have PAKS for the Consolidated SOftware Distribution +
> more). I had no problem with our USR and BASE pak that give us
> unlimited users. But with CDE installed, only root can log in, everyone else 
> gets "Too many user logged in." messages?

CDE is broken under 3.2D.  One of the 3.2c patches that was rolled into the 
kernel (OSF350-004) causes the CDE-ADK to break; I discovered this on 3.2c
and was able to trace the problem (with the help for Jeff Ford from Digital's
CSC) to the aforementioned patch.  That patch is part of 3.2d; hence 3.2d
doesn't work with the CDE ADK.

There is an unofficial patch available for dtlogin that fixes the problem;
it's not part of the standard patch list but you may be able to get it from
your CSC.  The call ID I opened (back in December) was C951212-3957.

4.0 showed up here today; perhaps you should wait for that... :-)

Tim
