On ANY C2 system, if you can't figure out how to bypass auditing when
you have root privs, then you don't know enough about that system.  Once
privileged, you can modify anything on the system.  If there is some
kind of non-eraseable media holding the log, you can at least detect the
changes, but if it's on a normal disk, then you (as root) can change it
at will.  As I see it, Digital is just being honest.  Perhaps the other
systems you are thinking about just don't admit the obvious.

