: 
: 
: The programs I used, compiled using DEC C, ran faster than compiled 
: using other compilers.  
: 
: Other factors that influenced my choice of compiler:
: 
: -  there is a tendency among "freeware" (and related) programs to 
: take explicit advantage of GCC-specific features.  Just adapting 
: makefiles is hard if people use exotic features of a compiler.  
: Case in point: compilers for high-level languages (e.g. Mercury)
: that generate GNU C code as portable assembler. Other case: SP.
: 
: -  a big advantage of Digital's compilers are options like -taso
: and xtaso,  especially if you're in a hurry to get a port done ..

Our experiences with gcc VS cc on DUX 3.2d correlates with the above.

We find that we NEED BOTH compilers every day.  Some off the net work
compiles best (or only) with gmake/gcc.  Our in house work often goes
best with with gmake/cc.  Some of our in house SW does run faster with
gcc than cc.  

