In article <4p4kca$1ng@galaxy.ucr.edu>,
System PRIVILEGED Account <root@ultrix.uor.edu> wrote:
>I am trying to write an add-multiuser script for for osf3.2d and it works 
>alright, but I haven't been able to figure out the "u_oldcrypt" field in 
>the /tcb/files/auth/? files and how it corresponds to crypt or crypt16, 
>or if it affects something else.  Anybody know?

See the AUTH_PROT_* constants in <prot.h> for which algorithm is which:
0 is bigcrypt (the 8-chars-at-a-time-with-salt-passed-along algorithm),
1 is crypt16 (the old Ultrix two-chunk munger). The u_oldcrypt field is
the algorithm in which the current password is encrypted; the u_newcrypt
field is the algorithm in which a new password for the account will be
encrypted. Typically, the only need for either of those fields is to set
u_oldcrypt to be 1 when migrating across encyrpted passwords from Ultrix.

--Malcolm

