In <4p9kis$6sg@netnews.upenn.edu> ggrevera@gradin.cis.upenn.edu (George Grevera) writes:

>Hi.  I seem to have tons of swap space but can't malloc a measly
>135M.  The particulars are 96M of physical memory on a DEC 3000
>running OSF1 V3.0.  I don't have a /sbin/swapdefault file.

You've been bitten by the default datasize limit:

    ues5:~ 170> limit datasize
    datasize        131072 kbytes
    ues5:~ 171> limit datasize unlimited
    ues5:~ 172> limit datasize
    datasize        1048576 kbytes

So, without further system tuning you can get as much as 1 GB of virtual
memory space for your process, but the default is set at 128 MB.

Dan
