> Why do mounted CDs (mount -t cdfs) show the version information on the
> ends of all the files (i.e the file looks like README.TXT;1 instead of
> README.TXT).
> 
> Is there any way to turn this off?
> 
> (DEC Alpha 3000, OSF/1 V3.0B (Rev 358.78))Check the man page for mount. The option you want to use is -o noversion. 
Additionally, the following item may be useful:

If a CD has RockRidge file extensions, use the -o rrip option instead. Just 
this weekend, I was attempting to export a RedHat Linux disk across my LAN. 
Using just -o noversion did not show the proper file names. For example, the 
directory RedHat showed up as redhat. Additionally, file names were truncated 
in the "8x3" DOS format. Changing the mount option to use RockRidge extensions 
fixed it all.

