In article <DsFruw.Err@solair1.inter.NL.net> Pim van der Eijk <pvde@nedernet.nl> writes:
>
>GCC was faster than the default (mips-originated) C compiler.

Only rarely true in my experience. Often due to the fact that GCC
defaults to ANSI mode and the normal CC defaults to K&R mode. Specifying
c89 or cc -std1 usually made cc faster.

>GEM-based C (cc -migrate) was slightly faster than GCC.

GEM-based C (or DEC C) is the default compiler under Digital UNIX V4.0
and will always kill the two others on anything containing floating point
and most of the time on integer code. Be sure to get a recent version,
it got a lot better since V3.2A.

