In article <4oi7d8$rle@glitnir.ifi.uio.no> torstenk@ifi.uio.no (Torsten Robert Kirschner) writes:

> >>>>> "DP" == David Phan <dphan@alpha.comsource.net> writes:
> In article <4ofqqd$alm@alpha.comsource.net> dphan@alpha.comsource.net (David Phan) writes:
> DP> I tried to link the library file /usr/local/sql/lib/libsql.a to a
> DP> C program myprog.c with the following command and got error messages:
> DP> cc /usr/local/sql/lib/libsql.a myprog.c
> 
> I'd suggest:
> 
> 	cc -L/usr/local/sql/lib -lsql myprog.c
> 
> In general, a look at cc's man page might be a good idea. Also, if you
> need header files, you might  have to add a -I/usr/local/sql/include.

True-ish.

Your version should be
	cc myprog.c -L/usr/local/sql/lib -lsql

David's version should be
	cc myprog.c /usr/local/sql/lib/libsql.a

(the linker doesn't know what it needs from libsql.a until it's read
myprog.o).

