In article <Ds7zG1.G7H@emr1.emr.ca>, cote@seismo.emr.ca (Tim Cote) writes:

> So how do I set up the X windows server to come up in 24 bit mode?

Edit /var/X11/xdm/Xservers. You'll see a line like:

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice -2

Add -vclass TrueColor eg:

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice 2 -vclass TrueColor

Stop and restart the Xserver by either rebooting or /sbin/init.d/xdm stop. Then
login as root on the console and restart using /sbin/init.d/xdm start ; exit

Should work fine,

Mark Parsons
