Freedom Series are deskside units (I know, I was using the first one
in the UK! The top end Freedom box (3400 or 3800 the one with 8 DSP
daughtercards anyway) is significantly faster the an RE2 and also
rather cheaper. SGI wins hands down on software support.

Then again Freedoms are available for RS/6000, Alpha, Sun, and I think
HP. And the always used to come in cheaper (they were about 70K when
RE2 Onyx were 100-150K

>The last I've seen advertised is a AlphaVME-based graphic processor. For
>"virtual reality" etc purposes even with multiple boards (ie processors). 
>Raw Alpha CPU power just used as a graphics device.....probably blows 
>any Sillycon Graphics toy to the moon....

You'd be quite wrong there then. The point of thing like Freedom,
RealityEngine & RE2, and PixelFlow is that operations are massively
parallel. Small numbers of powerful processors cannot compete in an
area that is highly susceptible to parallelism.

You're talking about 2D accelerators with software 3D running on a
fast CPU, I guess. This will never be faster than hardware accelerated
3D graphics. IIRC RE2's have several hundred pixel processor, 8 i860
with separate memories, etc in the pipeline. Also pipeline is a
keyword here...

