Hi,

   I'm trying to add a 3.5GB disk that was formerly residing
on an SGI Indigo to an Alpha 2100. I'm having trouble
reading (even zeroing) the disklabel. The device is rz3, 
which I created with MAKEDEV. When I enter

                  disklabel -z rz3

I get the following message

     disklabel: /dev/rrz3a: I/O error

Same message when I try to read or write a new disklabel.
Any suggestions out there what I should try. The device
does show up at boot up as present, and also shows as present
when I enter a sizer command, so I believe the connections
are OK.

