Hi All!

I think there is one little problem with my sendmail config. Mail gets 
sent out to other systems just fine. One server (homer) is both my DNS
and mail server. If I have a named.hosts record 
" IN MX 5 homer.networkss.com" then sendmail (when receiving mail) 
gives the error:

sendmail....: MX list for networkss.com. points back to homer.networkss.com

If I remove the MX entry and have no MX, sendmail (receiving mail) says:

sendmail....: networkss.com. config error: mail loops back to me (MX problem?)

I am sending mail (from the Internet) to an account on this particular
mail server, so I thought the mail is supposed to loop back to "me" ? 
Any ideas? It is a similar error using either the my native sendmail, 
or the BSD 8.7.5 sendmail.

